    "chunk_text": "IMF announcement on tranches takes CSE from gloom to light\n\nAlthough the CSE was enveloped in some negativity at the beginning of trading yesterday, later some positive trends were noted when the government announced that IMF had decided to release the 5th and 6th tranches of its package of assistance amounting to US$ 700 million soon.\n\nAt the end of the session the All Share Price Index was up by 72.89 points, while the S and P SL20 went down by 18.90 points. Turnover stood at Rs 1.88 billion with six crossings.\n\nwhich crossed 400,000 shares to the tune of Rs 133.4 million and its shares traded at Rs 333.50, HNB 180,000 shares crossed for Rs 71.2 million; its shares sold at Rs 395.50, Galle Face Capital Partners 2.7 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 70.2 million; its shares traded at Rs 26, hZenid two million shares crossed for Rs 38 million; its shares traded at Rs 19, DFCC 250,000 shares crossed for Rs 35 million; its shares sold at Rs 139.50 and Central Finance 100,000 shares crossed for Rs 22.5 million; its shares traded at Rs 225.\n\nIn the retail market top seven companies that mainly contributed to the turnover were; NDB Rs 455 million (4.1 million shares traded), Tokyo Cement (Non-Voting) Rs 72.5 million (one million shares traded), Commercial Bank Rs 51 million (253,000 shares traded), Acme Printers Rs 49.7 million (7.9 million shares traded), JKH Rs 49.1 million (2.6 million shares traded), HNB (Non-Voting) Rs 45 million (226,000 shares traded) and Chevron Lubricant Rs 40.7 million (226,000 shares traded).\n\nDuring the day 48.7 million share volumes changed hands in 19156 transactions.\n\nIt is said that banking sector counters, especially HNB and NDB, led the market while the manufacturing sector, especially JKH, and construction sector counters, especially Tokyo Cement, performed well."
