    "chunk_text": "This is why the Supreme Court judgment matters. The State has now formally acknowledged what the residents of Kollonnawa always knew: that their fundamental rights were violated. It will not bring back the 32 people who died. It will not return the years lost to illness, fear, and grief. I am not certain whether this judgment fully answers the questions of injustice they raised back then, yet it recognises that the lives and lands of the people of Kollonnawa, mostly from non-prestigious backgrounds, matter.\n\n(The author is a researcher attached to the Social Scientists\u2019 Association)"
