    "chunk_text": "Capt. (Retd.) Jagmohan currently serves as Chairman and Managing Director of MDL. A Naval Architect from Cochin University of Science and Technology, he holds postgraduate and M.Tech qualifications in Naval Construction and Ocean Engineering from IIT Delhi and IIT Kharagpur. With over 25 years of distinguished service in the Indian Navy, he has held key assignments in the Directorate of Naval Design and Naval Dockyard, Mumbai. His prior roles include Director at Goa Shipyard Ltd., and Chief General Manager \u2013 Design at Garden Reach Shipbuilders and Engineers Ltd., (GRSE), where he oversaw complex warship projects for the Indian Navy and Coast Guard. His appointment underscores MDL\u2019s strategic commitment to infuse Colombo Dockyard PLC\u2019s Board with unparalleled expertise, strengthening governance, operational excellence, and sustained growth.\n\nVish Govindasamy has been nominated by MDL as their Nominee Director (Non-Executive/Non-Independent).\n\nSenthilverl Nandhanan has been nominated by Senthilverl Holdings Ltd., as their Nominee Director (Non-Executive/Non-Independent).\n\nWith over two decades of experience spanning the financial services, energy, fast-moving consumer goods (FMCG), and investment sectors, he currently serves as Non-Executive Director at Amana Bank PLC and Sarvodaya Development Finance PLC, while leading operations as Executive Director at Senthilverl Holdings Ltd., and CEO of Dollar Corporation. He was the former Director of Panasian Power PLC (2017-2021). He holds an MBA from the University of Southern Queensland, Australia. Senthilverl brings a wealth of strategic insight and operational expertise, particularly in financial services and corporate governance."
