    "chunk_text": "What happened to my noble Profession?\n\nAnother incident that is etched in my memory also relates to Dr Karunaratna. I happened to be in his surgery when a poor lady brought her sick child. Having seen and dispensed the drugs free, Dr Karunaratna advised her to give Horlicks when she told him that she had no money to buy. Dr Karunaratne immediately turned to his dispenser and requested him to get a bottle from a shop nearby. What I remember vividly is his reply when the dispenser asked whether to buy a small bottle or a big one: \u201cWhat is the point in giving a small one?\u201d True to his name, he was an exquisite gem of kindness, and he leads the list of those who inspired me, for my chosen long career.\n\nUnlike many who opt for medicine as a career due to parental pressure, I did so because that happened to be my dream job. In fact, rather unexpectedly, I had to overcome objections from my father to do so. He wanted me to study both Arts and Science, like the famous philosopher educationist, Dr E W Adikaram. He suggested that I aim to join the Ceylon Civil Service; perhaps, the politician in him wanted\u00a0his son to become a permanent secretary to a ministry! On the other hand, I dreamt of being a doctor, maybe because of my earliest memories of my parents telling me about the medical problems I had in infancy and the heroic efforts of the doctors who saved my life."
  },
