    "chunk_size_bytes": 1716,
    "chunk_text": "41st Colombo Shopping Festival opens at BMICH\n\nThe 41st edition of the Colombo Shopping Festival (CSF) \u2013 Avurudu Fair is now on at the BMICH Exhibition Centre, offering days of festive shopping in celebration of the Sinhala and Tamil New Year.\n\nThe ceremonial opening commenced with the traditional lighting of the oil lamp on 8 April 2026, in the presence of distinguished guests, industry leaders, and invitees. Organised by Aitken Spence Conventions and Exhibitions, the event continues to reinforce its position as one of Sri Lanka\u2019s premier consumer exhibitions.\n\nRunning from 8\u201312 April 2026, from 10:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m. daily, the Colombo Shopping Festival brings together over 200 Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) from across the island, offering a vibrant marketplace that supports local businesses while delivering exceptional value to shoppers.\n\nThis year\u2019s Avurudu Fair promises an unmatched retail experience, featuring a wide range of products, including fashion, lifestyle, homeware, beauty, and more. Visitors can shop top brands such as Boss, EL Holdings, Vantage, Miniso, Governor Shirts, Edge Casual, Avirate, Cetaphil, Phoenix, Rite Shu, and many more, alongside a diverse selection of Indian stalls offering exclusive collections at significant discounts.\n\nThe festival creates an opportunity for families and shoppers to prepare for the New Year with deals, festive offers, and a lively atmosphere filled with seasonal excitement.\n\nWith its strong legacy and continued commitment to empowering local entrepreneurs, the Colombo Shopping Festival stands as a key highlight in Sri Lanka\u2019s event calendar, bringing together commerce, culture, and celebration under one roof."
