    "chunk_id": "2026-04-10-dailyftlk-a11e9c58-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "9842c8c18b7133df57aa5afcfe0195ab",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1920,
    "chunk_text": "Hayleys completes 800kW solar project  for LSEG Sri Lanka\n\nHayleys Solar, Sri Lanka\u2019s No.1 solar solutions provider, has successfully completed an 800kW rooftop installation for London Stock Exchange Group (LSEG), marking a significant milestone in the country\u2019s corporate renewable energy landscape.\n\nDelivered within an impressive two-month period, the installation covers six buildings and features 1,412 high-efficiency solar panels. The system is expected to generate an estimated 1,250 MWh of clean energy annually, supplying close to 80% of LSEG\u2019s daytime electricity needs and reducing carbon emissions by approximately 850 tonnes per year, the equivalent of removing nearly 185 petrol-powered cars from the road every year or planting more than 14,000 mature trees.\n\nThe project involved complex engineering requirements, including extensive underground cabling across an active corporate site. Hayleys Solar executed the installation with a zero-accident record, maintaining strict safety and operational standards throughout.\n\nCommenting on the project, Roshane Perera, Executive Director and Chief Executive Officer of Hayleys Solar, stated: \u201cPartnerships with ESG-conscious organisations are vital in accelerating Sri Lanka\u2019s transition to sustainable energy. We are grateful to LSEG for placing their trust in Hayleys Solar. This project is about providing reliable, sustainable energy solutions that enable Sri Lankan businesses to compete confidently on the global stage with a reduced carbon footprint.\u201d\n\nLSEG Group Director Site Lead - Malabe Feroz Cader said: \u201cAs one of the world\u2019s leading providers of financial markets infrastructure, delivering financial data, analytics, news and index across over 170 countries, LSEG takes its environmental responsibilities seriously. This collaboration with Hayleys Solar marks a significant step in our ongoing commitment to sustainability.\u201d"
  },
