    "chunk_size_bytes": 1453,
    "chunk_text": "SriLankan Airlines issues further warnings\n\nSriLankan Airlines wishes to inform the public of a serious escalation in ongoing scam activities targeting passengers and potential customers.\n\nThe airline has identified incidents of individuals impersonating SriLankan Airlines staff, including via WhatsApp and direct phone calls. During these interactions, scammers may request recipients to install mobile applications, share their screen or disclose one-time passwords (OTPs), banking PINs, credit card details or other sensitive financial information.\n\nSriLankan Airlines does not contact customers via WhatsApp or make unsolicited calls for ticketing, promotions or any other purpose. The airline will never request OTPs, banking PINs, credit card details, or any confidential information, nor will it ask customers to share screens or install mobile applications.\n\nCustomers are strongly advised to remain vigilant and to disregard and report any such communication to the relevant authorities.\n\nPassengers and the general public are urged to verify all promotions, offers and communications through the airline\u2019s official website www.srilankan.com or its verified social media channels.\n\nSri Lanka secures IMF staff-level deal for USD 700 million tranche\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
