    "chunk_text": "CEAT Kelani adjudged best-managed company in Sri Lanka\n\nCEAT Kelani Holdings shared the overall Gold award for Best Management Practices and was honoured with four other significant accolades at the 2026 edition of the Best Management Practices Company Awards of the Institute of Chartered Professional Managers of Sri Lanka (CPM Sri Lanka), to be adjudged the country\u2019s best-managed company.\n\nThe company also received the Sector Award as Winner in the Manufacturing (Tyre & Rubber) category, was ranked among the \u2018Forty Outstanding Companies\u2019 at the awards, and was presented a Best Management Practices Excellence Award. In addition, CEAT Kelani Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer Ravi Dadlani was recognised with the Leadership Excellence award, underscoring the strength of the company\u2019s leadership and strategic direction.\n\nThe CPM Best Management Practices Company Awards recognise public and private sector organisations for excellence in management across leadership, policies and strategies, people management, partnerships and resources, processes and performance, based on the year under review.\n\nCommenting on the awards, CEAT Kelani Managing Director & CEO Ravi Dadlani said: \u201cTo be named the best-managed company in Sri Lanka is an extraordinary honour as well as a reward for years of hard work in times of challenge. This recognition reflects the company\u2019s sustained focus on embedding best-in-class management practices across its operations with the involvement of employees at every level.\u201d\n\nColombo Shopping Festival 2026 declared open for 5 days of Avurudu Shopping\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
