    "chunk_text": "That was the first time I enjoyed a traditional village Avurudu celebration. One incident that is etched in my memory is how Ran Banda who wanted to show off his good looks climbed a jambu tree and started plucking the fruits for the girls. Then came a BRRRR sound and with the broken branch down came Ran Banda. He felt so awkward that he disappeared from the scene. Not truthfully, but politely everybody applauded.\n\nAuspicious times were observed to the letter. One such important custom was people having their heads anointed with a medicinal decoction, whilst standing on some special leaves under a branch of a particular tree. The person applying the oil was a respected elder, often the chief monk of the village temple.\n\nBlessings here are reciprocal and very comforting as one is blessed with good health, good fortune and long life. One sure fact is that at this season people wish each other the best of everything in the year to come.\n\nChamara Kala Nikethanaya Marks Golden Milestone with Grand \u2018Sheershabharana Ordination\u2019 Ceremony\n\nForever Hero Herath: Remembering a JVP Sahodaraya on the 55th Anniversary\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
